  "title": "When Fire Technology Goes Quiet, Value Becomes Clear",
  "summary": "For today’s fire departments, access to information is just as important as access to physical equipment. Responders rely on technology to deliver incident details, location data, building information, and other critical insights that help them make informed decisions on every call. Although the department’s contingency plans kept communications operational, firefighters suddenly found themselves without many of the digital tools they used every day. We still had our radios, but...",
